arametrically as\n\n$$\nx = 4\\cos\\theta, \\,\\,\\, y = 2\\sin\\theta, \\quad 0\\leq \\theta <     2\\pi,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\leq\\theta <  2\\pi,$ we have $-1 \\leq \\cos{\\theta} \\leq 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -4 & \\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 4 \\\\ -4 & \\le x\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-4 \\leq x \\leq 4.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\leq\\theta <  2\\pi,$ we have $-1 \\leq \\sin{\\theta} \\leq 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -2 & \\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 2 \\\\ -2 & \\le y\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-2 \\leq y \\leq 2.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $-4 \\leq x \\leq 4$ and $-2 \\leq y \\leq 2.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049872}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698269 :question-generator/id #uuid "1630b798-b9bc-596e-8d7a-1af860fe14eb" :question-generator/script "generators/a6/a644b3a2ec0622886416ffe401885d8cfd2ba86873b726c50641589810ba9755/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088029} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088281} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233713} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233838} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259561} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292915} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302364} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302365} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302367} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302369} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302370} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338790} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342038} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342042} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400121} {:db/id 